---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/astro/Footer.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Terms of Use - PantryPal"
  description="Terms of Use for the PantryPal app for iPhone and Android: the licence, AI and food-safety limits, the free plan, PantryPal Pro subscriptions and free trial, refunds, and your rights."
  canonical="https://coachie-ai.com/terms-of-use-pantrypal"
  ogTitle="Terms of Use - PantryPal"
  ogDescription="The agreement between you and the publisher of PantryPal."
  noIndex={false}
>
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 mb-8">The agreement between you and the publisher of PantryPal</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Effective date: 27 September 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">Last updated: 27 September 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-8">

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern your use of the PantryPal mobile app ("PantryPal", "the app"), published by <strong>Veera</strong>, an individual developer based in India ("we", "us", "our"). By downloading or using PantryPal you agree to these Terms and to our <a href="/privacy-policy-pantrypal" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 1. Who can use PantryPal -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Who can use PantryPal</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>You must be at least 13 years old.</li>
          <li>If you are under 18 (or the age of majority where you live), you may use PantryPal only with the permission of a parent or guardian, who agrees to these Terms on your behalf and is responsible for any purchase.</li>
          <li>You must not use PantryPal if you are barred from doing so under the laws of India or the country you live in.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. What PantryPal does -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. What PantryPal does</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          PantryPal helps you keep track of the food you have at home. You can add food by photo, receipt, barcode or by hand, see what should be used first, keep a shopping list, get recipe ideas built from your pantry, and cook step by step with timers, read-aloud and optional voice commands. There is no account: your data is stored on your phone, as described in the <a href="/privacy-policy-pantrypal" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Licence to use the app -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">3. Licence to use the app</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          We grant you a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use PantryPal on devices you own or control, for your own non-commercial use, in line with these Terms and the rules of the App Store or Google Play you downloaded it from. You must not:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>copy, modify, resell, rent or distribute the app, or make it available to others as a service;</li>
          <li>reverse engineer, decompile or try to extract the source code, except where the law expressly allows it;</li>
          <li>bypass or interfere with the free plan limits, subscription checks or security features;</li>
          <li>use the app, or its connection to our AI and data providers, to send anything other than photos and information about food for your own household;</li>
          <li>upload content that is illegal, harmful, or that shows other people without their permission;</li>
          <li>use the app in any way that breaks the law or harms us, other users or our service providers.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. AI features and food safety -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">4. AI features and food safety</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          PantryPal uses artificial intelligence, provided by OpenAI, to recognise food in photos and receipts and to write recipes. It also estimates freshness ("Use today", "use soon") and nutrition. <strong>These results are generated automatically and can be wrong or incomplete.</strong> In particular:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Scanning can miss food, name it incorrectly or get quantities wrong. Always review the results before saving them.</li>
          <li>Freshness and "Use today" hints are rough estimates based on typical shelf life. They are not a guarantee that food is safe to eat. Always check the food itself, its label and its use-by date, and follow food safety guidance.</li>
          <li>Recipes try to respect your diets and allergies, but <strong>may still contain allergens or ingredients you cannot eat</strong>. Always read every ingredient and product label before cooking and eating, especially if you or someone you cook for has a food allergy or intolerance.</li>
          <li>Nutrition figures, cooking times and temperatures are estimates. Make sure food, especially meat, poultry, fish and eggs, is cooked thoroughly.</li>
          <li>Product details from barcode scans come from Open Food Facts, an open database edited by volunteers, and may be inaccurate.</li>
          <li>PantryPal does not give medical, dietary or nutritional advice. If you have a medical condition or special dietary needs, ask a qualified professional.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          You are responsible for deciding what to buy, store, cook and eat. You use AI results at your own risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Your content -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">5. Your content</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          The photos you scan and the items, lists and notes you enter ("your content") remain yours. You give us, and the service providers named in the <a href="/privacy-policy-pantrypal" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">Privacy Policy</a>, permission to process your content only as needed to run the features you use, for example sending a photo to OpenAI to identify food. You confirm that you have the right to use any photo you scan. PantryPal does not store your photos.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Free plan and PantryPal Pro -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">6. Free plan and PantryPal Pro</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3">6.1 Free plan</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          PantryPal is free to download. The free plan includes a limited number of photo scans and recipe sets each month, and fewer recipes per set, as shown in the app. We may change the free plan's limits from time to time.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">6.2 Pro subscription</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>PantryPal Pro is an auto-renewing subscription, offered monthly or yearly. It unlocks unlimited scans and recipe sets, receipt scanning, recipe filters, more recipes per set and hands-free voice cooking. The current features and price in your currency are shown in the app and the store before you buy.</li>
          <li>Payment is charged to your Apple ID or Google Play account when you confirm the purchase, or at the end of a free trial.</li>
          <li><strong>The subscription renews automatically</strong> for the same period and price unless you cancel it at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. Your account is charged for renewal within the 24 hours before the period ends.</li>
          <li>You can manage or cancel your subscription at any time in your App Store or Google Play account settings (in PantryPal: <strong>Settings &gt; Manage subscription</strong>). Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription. After cancelling, Pro stays active until the end of the period you have paid for.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">6.3 Free trial</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The yearly plan may include a <strong>3-day free trial</strong> for new subscribers, if the store shows it as available to you. Only one free trial is available per Apple ID or Google account. Unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends, the subscription starts and the yearly price is charged when the trial ends. If you cancel during a trial, Pro ends when the trial ends. Any unused part of a free trial is forfeited when you buy a subscription.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">6.4 Prices, changes and refunds</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Prices can differ by country and may include taxes. We may change subscription prices. Apple or Google will tell you in advance, and where required ask for your agreement, before a new price applies at renewal.</li>
          <li>Purchases are handled by Apple or Google, so refunds are decided by them under their refund policies. For the App Store, request a refund at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. For Google Play, see Google Play's refund policy or your order history. Nothing in these Terms limits any right to a refund you have under the consumer law of your country.</li>
          <li>If you change devices, use <strong>Restore purchase</strong> in the app, signed in with the same Apple ID or Google account.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Third-party services -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">7. Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          PantryPal relies on services from OpenAI, Google (Firebase), Open Food Facts, Apple and Google Play. Your use of those services may also be subject to their own terms. We are not responsible for their availability or content, and a feature that depends on one of them may stop working if that service changes or becomes unavailable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Availability and changes to the app -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">8. Availability and changes to the app</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          We work to keep PantryPal useful and reliable, but we do not promise that it will always be available, uninterrupted or error-free. Many features need an internet connection. We may add, change or remove features, or stop offering the app, at any time. If we stop offering Pro while you have an active paid subscription, you can cancel it and ask the store for a refund of the unused period.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Intellectual property -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">9. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          PantryPal, including its design, text, graphics, illustrations and code, belongs to us or our licensors and is protected by intellectual property laws. These Terms do not give you any rights in our name or logo. The app includes open-source software and fonts used under their own licences. Recipes generated for you are provided for your personal use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Feedback -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">10. Feedback</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          If you send us ideas or suggestions, for example by email, you allow us to use them to improve PantryPal without any obligation to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Disclaimer -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">11. Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, PantryPal is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not guarantee that AI results, freshness estimates, nutrition information or product data are accurate or complete. Some countries do not allow certain warranties to be excluded, so some of these exclusions may not apply to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Limitation of liability -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">12. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, or for loss of data, food, profits or goodwill, arising from your use of PantryPal, including any illness, allergic reaction or injury resulting from food you choose to buy, store, prepare or eat. Our total liability to you for any claim relating to PantryPal is limited to the amount you paid us for PantryPal Pro in the 12 months before the claim arose.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited by law, such as liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or your statutory rights as a consumer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 13. Indemnity -->
